  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3742",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits, specifically Kcnv2, Kcna7, and Kcnc3, through a common mechanism of binding. These subunits are involved in the delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, which is a critical process in cellular electrophysiology. The shared involvement of these subunits in the same functional pathway suggests a potential overlap in their roles, possibly in regulating cellular potassium homeostasis. The high scores from the three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Guanidine and Kcna6, likely through the indirect pathway of their participation in the delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that Guanidine may influence Kcna6 through its interaction with these potassium channel subunits, thereby affecting the function of the delayed rectifier potassium channel. The mechanism is supported by the overlapping functional roles of the subunits, suggesting a possible regulatory or modulatory effect of Guanidine on Kcna6.",
